{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789867519,"nonce":"4WIuOdYB/Qn4obzgH8S7YElh7mw=","message":"Note from the schema design (7c90fbd, decided 2026-09-19): the flow catalogue shares the schema's storage machinery. Flows are essentially named aliases, and they want the same things the schema does — to travel with the tracker rather than a branch, and to merge when two people edit different entries.\n\nSo flows live as a config entity in the `work` namespace alongside the schema, with per-key ops (DefineFlow/RemoveFlow). That sharing is part of why the CRDT entity won over a plain blob: the op machinery is amortized across both. Worth knowing before this issue settles the verb catalogue.","files":null}]}